Relevant columns / elements and how they will be used  

• `Sides.Side` : keep only `'LONG'` side trades.  
• `Sides.PartyIDs.PartyID` : look for the string that hints at the trading strategy;  
  – `LOWER(PartyID) LIKE '%momo%'` → momentum strategy  
  – `LOWER(PartyID) LIKE '%luck%'` → feeling‑lucky strategy  
• `StrikePrice` and `LastPx` : intrinsic value is taken as (`StrikePrice - LastPx`).  
• (optionally) `Quantity` : could be used for a size‑weighted version, but is not required for the plain average asked for.  

Typical filter / join conditions that will be reused  

```
UNNEST(Sides)        AS s
UNNEST(s.PartyIDs)   AS p
WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
```

and for strategy tagging  

```
CASE
  WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momo%' THEN 'momentum'
  WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%luck%' THEN 'feeling-lucky'
END  AS strategy
```

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory → final queries (each capped with LIMIT 20 unless naturally fewer)

```sql
-- 1. Peek at a handful of raw rows
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Distinct PartyID strings so we know what text to search for
SELECT DISTINCT p.PartyID
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
     UNNEST(Sides)      AS s,
     UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) AS p
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. PartyIDs that look like momentum or feeling‑lucky
SELECT DISTINCT p.PartyID
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
     UNNEST(Sides)      AS s,
     UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) AS p
WHERE LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momo%'   -- momentum
   OR LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%luck%'   -- feeling‑lucky
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Compute intrinsic value for every long‑side leg
SELECT s.Side,
       p.PartyID,
       StrikePrice - LastPx AS intrinsic_value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
     UNNEST(Sides)      AS s,
     UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) AS p
WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Tag each long‑side leg as momentum / feeling‑lucky / other
SELECT
  CASE
    WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momo%' THEN 'momentum'
    WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%luck%' THEN 'feeling-lucky'
    ELSE 'other'
  END AS strategy,
  StrikePrice - LastPx AS intrinsic_value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
     UNNEST(Sides)      AS s,
     UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) AS p
WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Average intrinsic value per strategy (all strategies shown)
SELECT
  CASE
    WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momo%' THEN 'momentum'
    WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%luck%' THEN 'feeling-lucky'
    ELSE 'other'
  END AS strategy,
  AVG(StrikePrice - LastPx) AS avg_intrinsic
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
     UNNEST(Sides)      AS s,
     UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) AS p
WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
GROUP BY strategy
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Same as #6 but show only momentum vs feeling‑lucky
SELECT
  CASE
    WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momo%' THEN 'momentum'
    WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%luck%' THEN 'feeling-lucky'
  END AS strategy,
  AVG(StrikePrice - LastPx) AS avg_intrinsic
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
     UNNEST(Sides)      AS s,
     UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) AS p
WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
  AND (LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momo%' OR LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%luck%')
GROUP BY strategy
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Difference in average intrinsic value (feeling‑lucky minus momentum)
SELECT
  MAX(CASE WHEN strategy = 'feeling-lucky' THEN avg_intrinsic END)
  - MAX(CASE WHEN strategy = 'momentum'     THEN avg_intrinsic END)
    AS diff_intrinsic
FROM (
  SELECT
    CASE
      WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momo%' THEN 'momentum'
      WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%luck%' THEN 'feeling-lucky'
    END AS strategy,
    AVG(StrikePrice - LastPx) AS avg_intrinsic
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
       UNNEST(Sides)      AS s,
       UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) AS p
  WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
    AND (LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momo%' OR LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%luck%')
  GROUP BY strategy
) 
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. A one‑shot conditional aggregation version (same logic as #8)
SELECT
  AVG(CASE WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%luck%' THEN StrikePrice - LastPx END)
  - AVG(CASE WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momo%' THEN StrikePrice - LastPx END)
    AS diff_intrinsic
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
     UNNEST(Sides)      AS s,
     UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) AS p
WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
  AND (LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momo%' OR LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%luck%')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL answer: how much higher is the feeling‑lucky average vs momentum
SELECT
  ROUND(
    AVG(CASE WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%luck%' THEN StrikePrice - LastPx END)
    - AVG(CASE WHEN LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momo%' THEN StrikePrice - LastPx END)
  , 4) AS avg_intrinsic_diff
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
     UNNEST(Sides)      AS s,
     UNNEST(s.PartyIDs) AS p
WHERE s.Side = 'LONG'
  AND (LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%momo%' OR LOWER(p.PartyID) LIKE '%luck%');
```

Run the last query to obtain the numerical difference – i.e., the average intrinsic value (StrikePrice − LastPx) of long‑side trades that carry a “feeling‑lucky” PartyID minus the corresponding average for “momentum” PartyIDs.
